# shell builtins: part of the command surface, but not busybox applets, so they
# never appear in `busybox --list`.
#
# this list is NOT hand-maintained any more. it was, and it silently went stale
# the moment busybox.config.features turned on alias/getopts/jobs -- seven live
# builtins that nothing documented and no gate noticed, because the gate only
# checked the names someone had remembered to write down.
#
# G24 now derives the truth from two places that cannot both be wrong: the
# builtin table in the pinned ash.c, filtered by what the BUILT binary reports
# for `type NAME`. this file must equal that set exactly, in both directions.
. : [ alias bg break cd chdir command continue echo eval exec exit
export false fg getopts hash history jobs kill let local printf pwd
read readonly return set shift test times trap true type ulimit umask
unalias unset wait